            2. How We Picked
          </h2>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What Our Picks Are Based On</h3>

          <p>
            We did not run these tools through a season of hands-on testing, and we are not going to pretend we did. These picks are built from manufacturer specifications, published cutting capacities, materials and warranty terms, replacement parts lists, and the long-running owner reports that exist for tools that have been on the market for years. Several of these designs, the Felco 2 in particular, have been sold in essentially the same form for decades, which means there is an unusually deep record of how they hold up and what wears out first.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">The Four Things We Weighted</h3>

          <p>
            We weighted four things most heavily. Construction came first: whether the working head is forged or stamped, what steel it uses, and how the head joins the handle, since that joint is where cheap tools fail. Serviceability came second: whether blades, springs and handles can be replaced, and whether the edge can be resharpened at home with a file or stone. Third was the warranty, and specifically what it covers, because a lifetime warranty on a handle is not the same as a lifetime warranty on a blade. Fourth was fit, including hand size and handedness.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What We Excluded</h3>

          <p>
            We excluded tools whose claims we could not check against a maker page, spec sheet or a consistent run of retailer listings. Where sources disagree, as they do on the exact weight of the Felco 2 and the blade length of some hori-hori models, we give the figure the maker publishes or say that listings vary. We also avoided quoting prices beyond rough bands, because garden tool prices swing widely with season and seller, and a recommendation that hinges on a specific sale price is not much of a recommendation.
          </p>
        </div>

