          <p>
            A starter kit should be built around jobs, not tool categories. The jobs most yards present are planting and transplanting, digging new beds and dividing perennials, weeding, pruning shrubs and small trees, and cleanup. Each of the seven tools covers one of those jobs better than anything else, and several overlap usefully, so you are never stuck without something that works. The table below maps the job to the tool.
          </p>

