          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A good garden tool kit is small. Seven tools, chosen for forged heads, bypass blades, replaceable parts and a fit that suits your hands, will do more work than a boxed set several times the size, and most of them can be sharpened, rebuilt or repaired instead of replaced.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you are starting from nothing, buy the pruner, the gloves and either the hori-hori or the trowel this season, add the shovel and hoe when you dig your first bed, and pick up loppers when the shrubs need them. Take a few minutes to clean and oil them after use, and they will still be in the shed when the plants they put in the ground are fully grown.
